ent.get` in `weather.py` now retries when the server returns 503, making at most 3 attempts. I checked it against a local test server and every case behaved as intended.\n\n**How it works:**\n- The client catches `urllib.error.HTTPError`. If the code is 503 and attempts remain, it closes the error response, waits, and tries again.\n- The wait doubles each time: 0.5s after the first failure, 1s after the second.\n- Any status other than 503 is raised straight away, with no retry.\n- If the third attempt also gets a 503, that error is raised to the caller.\n- Two new constructor arguments, `max_attempts=3` and `backoff=0.5`, control the attempt count and the starting wait. Existing calls don't need to change.\n\n**Test results** (local HTTP server, `backoff=0.05`):\n\n| Server behaviour | Result | Requests made |\n|---|---|---|\n| Succeeds first time | `{'temp': 20}` | 1 |\n| 503 twice, then succeeds | `{'temp': 20}` | 3 |\n| 503 every time | `HTTPError 503` | 3 (waited 0.15s = 0.05 + 0.1) |\n| 500 once | `HTTPError 500` | 1 (no retry) |\n\nI didn't add a test file because the repo has no test setup.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": [], "params_stripped_requests": 0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 2, "replies_ok": 6, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 34691, "requests_cache_write": 177468, "requests_cost_usd": 0.9319341999999999, "requests_count": 6, "requests_input_uncached": 14, "requests_output": 1880, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "omp:trig-omp-netclient:claude-opus-5-5:trial9", "run_seed": 1016, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 77, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-20T03:48:13.392124+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "subagent_write_calls": 0, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 23.671, "t_checker_s": 2.431, "t_env_setup_s": 0.001, "task": "trig-omp-netclient", "task_calls": 0, "thinking_mode": "off", "thinking_sent": ["none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none"], "timeout_s